"""Reference-first production intent, without category questionnaires."""
BRIEF='''
SIMPLE REFERENCE STUDIO — reference image is the primary design specification.
Infer the output type, subject, historical periods, geographic levels and content inventory from the actual reference, not from a category default. Recreate its composition, proportions, grouping, silhouette, visual density, detailed drawing/photographic language, and all meaningful sub-drawings for the selected target project. Do not simplify into a basemap or impose exploded plates. Choose the target extent necessary for that narrative: historical city collages use city history, regional drawings use regional context, local details use the actual site. No automatic clipping to the local study boundary.
Inspect original images and detail crops before drawing. Write inferred_intent.md with the actual reference type, full content inventory, matching target subjects and evidence plan. For historical collage, locate authentic photographs/archival depictions of the TARGET CITY and relevant eras in project sources or reliable archives; verify dates/subjects and record provenance in separate source notes. Do not transplant the reference city's buildings or fabricate archival photography. Adapt verified assets into the reference's visual language. Missing evidence or unavailable image tools is a failed requirement, not permission to replace the scene with generic icons or omit it. Preserve source files.
For a full board, inventory every group and child diagram and preserve their relative positions and visual area; no module limit. For other references, preserve their actual drawing structure without inventing board panels. Mandatory project annotation rules still apply; explain necessary differences separately. Produce one complete refined result, PNG and PDF plus honest editable source where feasible. All delivered text is English. Inspect output against the original reference at sheet and detail scale, satisfy reference fidelity v5, and list unresolved departures honestly. All review_version fields must be 5.
'''
BRIEF += '\nMULTIPLE REFERENCES — when more than one visual reference is selected, their order is deliberate. The FIRST entry in Reference files / reference_order is the MAIN reference: it governs composition, drawing type, proportions, overall density, palette and line language. Later entries are SUPPORTING references for compatible, specific details only. Inspect every reference and record each role in reference_analysis.md. Do not average conflicting styles or assemble several complete reference layouts into a collage. Where secondary references conflict with the main reference, retain the main and document the conflict separately. All subjects must be freshly adapted to the target project using evidence. For Push retain the same original reference order and hierarchy. Target project board style sources, when present, govern only an explicitly requested project-style conversion, not new subject matter.\n'
PUSH='''
PUSH — repair reference fidelity, not a new interpretation. The ORIGINAL selected reference remains the authority. The previous output is a rejected candidate, not an approved style template. Compare it against the original at matching sizes and detailed crops; list the largest discrepancies in composition, content coverage, density, contrast, linework, photographic treatment and fine details. Rebuild deficient regions, recover omitted subject matter using verified target sources, and increase reference-matched substantive detail. Preserve correct project facts and geometry. You may substantially recompose instead of merely recolouring. Do not accumulate drift from earlier Push versions. Save push_review.md with concrete before/after evidence, remaining discrepancies and source limitations. Never claim an exact match unless the inspected result supports that claim. Keep earlier files untouched.
'''
def prepare(req,parent=None):
 if req.get('operation')=='push':
  if not parent:raise ValueError('Choose a result to Push.')
  import json
  old=json.loads(parent['request'])
  order=old.get('reference_order') or old.get('references',[])+old.get('sources',[])
  if not order:raise ValueError('This production has no original reference. Choose a reference first.')
  req={**req,'sources':old.get('sources',[]),'references':old.get('references',[]),'reference_order':order,'simple_reference':True}
 if not req.get('simple_reference'):return req
 if not (req.get('references') or req.get('sources')):raise ValueError('Choose a reference first.')
 return {**req,'recipe':None,'kind':'Reference-led drawing','alternative_count':1,'alternative_similarity':'close','detail_level':'rich','project_board_style':False,'geographic_scope':'custom','scope_details':'Infer evidence-backed target extent from the original reference narrative; include broader city/history/region where needed, without default local boundary clipping.','brief':BRIEF+(PUSH if req.get('operation')=='push' else '')}
